From c80a6ef2e2c8f34c66467c6b8417effaf3efa9fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Frdlik <michaelf.ms@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 23:19:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/22] Thylacine Warp V-3b-3b: the Venus vkCreateInstance
 bring-up backend

Turns the V-3b-3a vn_renderer skeleton into a working backend and drives a
real vkCreateInstance + physical-device enumeration over /srv/warp (Model B).
Verified on thyla-pi/KVM real V3D: 2 Venus devices ("Virtio-GPU Venus (V3D
4.2.14.0)"), create + enumerate + memory-props + destroy, boot green.

Backend (vn_renderer_thylacine.c): shmem_create mints a HOST3D ring on the
client's venus ctx (ring/new host3d) + weft-maps it; submit forwards opaque
venus bytes (vkCreateRingMESA bootstrap + doorbells) to ctx/<id>/submit;
wait/sync are a guest-side u64 timeline bound to the WARP ctx fence (teardown
only -- bring-up replies are pure ring-head polls); info reads the venus capset
(caps-venus). Transport (warp_client.c): the host3d-ring verbs + a raw
venus-submit + a venus-caps read, reusing warp_open + the issued/signaled fence
model. meson: warp_client.c + the winsys include dir into the venus lib.

wait is a BLOCKING Tread of ctx/<id>/fence (warp_fence_wait), NOT t_poll -- the
seam's qids carry no QTPOLL so t_poll would busy-spin (corrects WARP-V3-DESIGN
0.14's op table).

Audit (holotype Fable 5, 0 P0 / 1 P1 / 1 P2 / 4 P3):
  - F1 [P1]: ridx recycled a server slot the host retires only at ctx death ->
    permanent shmem_create failure after the first destroy. Interim fix:
    monotonic ridx (never freed) -> no reuse -> no deadlock; the per-ring
    destroy verb + regression test are owed at 3c.
  - F2 [P2]: the 8 MiB cs pool is dead against the 1 MiB ring ceiling ->
    #ifdef __thylacine__ clamp to 1 MiB in vn_instance.c.
  - F3 [P3]: timeline over-advertisement (submit drops ring_idx) -> report a
    single timeline; F4 [P3]: empty-cs batch binds syncs to the last issued
    seq; F5 [P3] wait ns-timeout tracked for 3c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
